{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"florid-gelatinous-doe","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py:169-172` — Preserve solver selection behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_external_canary.py:1-12` — Preserve external-tier canary selection and skip behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py:1-11` — Preserve the cloud-mutation integration workflow contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py:1-14, 35-41, 59-68, 147-154` — Preserve actionable external-mutation failure diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_external_tier_gate_ref.py:1-16, 46-52` — Preserve external-tier gate evaluation against the requested ref. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_external_tier_live_reachability.py:1-27, 60-68, 102-109` — Preserve live-tier reachability gating and safe skip/failure distinctions. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_extra_coverage_guard.py:1-21` — Preserve the extra-coverage regression guard. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py:1-19` — Preserve importability on platforms without fcntl. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py:1-21` — Preserve common-dir coordination across concurrent fetches. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py:125-128` — Preserve fidelity scoring at the selected boundary. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_file_tombstone_behavior_d064.py:1-19` — Preserve file-tombstone deletion and replay semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_first_request_window_f79d.py:1-18` — Preserve first-request window accounting. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_admission_heldout.py:1-10` — Preserve independent fixture-admission coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_admission.py:1-19, 249-260, 327-334` — Preserve fixture admission criteria and rejection diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_emit_heldout.py:1-20` — Preserve independent output-shape and escaping coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_emit.py:1-14` — Preserve canonical fixture emission semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_heal_heldout.py:1-10, 210-213, 216-218, 250-252, 266-268, 295-297, 315-318, 349-354, 386-389, 399-404, 426-430, 456-458, 477-481` — Preserve healing safety, idempotence, and malformed-input boundaries. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py:1-11` — Preserve fixture-healing behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py tests/unit/test_external_canary.py tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py tests/unit/test_external_tier_gate_ref.py tests/unit/test_external_tier_live_reachability.py tests/unit/test_extra_coverage_guard.py tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py tests/unit/test_file_tombstone_behavior_d064.py tests/unit/test_first_request_window_f79d.py tests/unit/test_fixture_admission_heldout.py tests/unit/test_fixture_admission.py tests/unit/test_fixture_emit_heldout.py tests/unit/test_fixture_emit.py tests/unit/test_fixture_heal_heldout.py tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"4ca9-4d50-1846-4960","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 11: eval_solver–fixture_heal"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571431907899558,"uuid":"1a3f7e16-b06d-456f-929d-b13dd8a03397"}